 "title": "Linux Kernel Approaching 2000 CVEs Per Release Driven by AI Analysis",
 "summary": "The Linux kernel is approaching 2000 CVEs per release, a significant increase from the ~500 CVEs typical of the Linux 6.x era. This surge is attributed to the mass application of AI and large language models for source code analysis. Maintainers must filter through a high volume of AI-generated findings, including low-priority fixes, cleanups, and potential hallucinations, to identify genuine security issues.",
